        "kind": "assessable",
        "relation": "narrower",
        "relation_rationale": "The article's month-9 LS percentage-change profile supplies every requested randomized dose-versus-placebo comparison without selecting the most favorable dose or inventing pooling. Its narrative reports reductions versus placebo of 6.8% (95% CI: -47.5%, 33.9%), 7.1% (95% CI: -51.3%, 37.1%), and 23.8% (95% CI: -65.7%, 18.1%) for 2-, 5-, and 9-dose regimens respectively; the positive reduction wording and signed intervals are retained without reinterpretation as ratio reductions. The selected group-bound tuple is the article's signed LS percentage changes. PPS restrictions make it narrower than all randomized Part 1 patients. The 24-month contrasts, absolute g/g changes in Table S3, and open-label Japanese Part 2 do not replace the 9-month comparative result. Current registry FAS log-ratio analysis is a material competing analysis, not historical replay or confirmation of the article model. No unique primary dose contrast is designated in the inspected sources; historical absence versus designation of a primary outcome remains unresolved despite the article/current registry primary labels.",
        "reported": {
          "analysis_population": "Article efficacy PPS: Part 1 n=41 (placebo 12, 2-dose 11, 5-dose 8, 9-dose 10), after seven exposure-based exclusions; observations after prohibited therapy were excluded. Month-9 counts total 39 (placebo 10, 2-dose 11, 5-dose 8, 9-dose 10). This is not all 48 randomized patients, and these counts do not prove complete ascertainment or all model inputs.",
